# Iceberg, Snowflake, and AWS reference links

When this project touches **Apache Iceberg**, **Snowflake Iceberg or catalog integration**, or **AWS (S3 Tables, Glue, IAM, Lake Formation)**, prefer the links below over ad hoc sources. Use them to verify APIs, configuration steps, and product behavior.

## Apache Iceberg

- [REST Catalog API (spec)](https://iceberg.apache.org/spec/#rest-catalog-api)
- [AWS integration](https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/aws/)

## Snowflake documentation

- [Iceberg tables](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-iceberg)
- [CREATE CATALOG INTEGRATION](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/create-catalog-integration)
- [Catalog integration with vended credentials](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-iceberg-configure-catalog-integration-vended-credentials)
- [Catalog integration with REST (Glue)](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/tables-iceberg-configure-catalog-integration-rest-glue)

## AWS documentation

- [Glue: connect to the Data Catalog using the Glue Iceberg REST endpoint](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/connect-glu-iceberg-rest.html) (endpoint URI, REST prefix / catalog ID patterns)
- [S3 Tables: Iceberg REST endpoint for open-source clients](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-tables-integrating-open-source.html) (separate **`s3tables.<region>.amazonaws.com/iceberg`** host and **`s3tables`** SigV4 signing name — contrast with Snowflake **Glue** REST integration)
- [S3 Tables getting started (tutorial — create bucket)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-tables-getting-started.html#s1-tables-tutorial-create-bucket)
- [What is AWS Glue?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/what-is-glue.html)
- [IAM roles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles.html)
- [S3 Tables with Glue (integrating Glue endpoint)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-tables-integrating-glue-endpoint.html)
- [What is AWS Lake Formation?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lake-formation/latest/dg/what-is-lake-formation.html)
- [S3 Tables API reference](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_s3tables.html)

